Q: How to make reflinks in PHP? A: <p>I don't think there is a PHP function which do it directly, but you may use <a href="https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.system.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">system</a> or <a href="https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.exec.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">exec</a> to execute a command on the underlying system:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

system('cp --reflink=always &lt;path1&gt; &lt;path2&gt;', $result_code);

// $result_code holds command execution return status
if ($result_code == 0) {
    // Success
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to toggle bootstrap nav pane from a button A: <p>Your main mistakes are:</p>
<ul>
<li>getElementById('#nav-volunteers') is wrong.</li>
<li>getElementById() takes the raw id, without #.</li>
<li>tabElement.show() is wrong because tabElement is just a DOM element.</li>
<li>In Bootstrap 5 you need a bootstrap.Tab instance, then call .show().</li>
<li>Your button uses data-bs-target=&quot;#nav-contact-tab&quot;, but there is no such tab pane or tab button in the markup you posted. That mismatch can trigger Bootstrap selector errors.</li>
<li>There is also a typo mismatch in your ids:
<ul>
<li><p>button id: nav-voluteers-tab</p>
</li>
<li><p>pane aria-labelledby: nav-volunteers-tab</p>
<p>Those should match exactly.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Also, if the goal is to switch to the Volunteering tab, you should target the tab button, not the pane.</p>
<p>Use this instead:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot; onclick=&quot;showTab()&quot;&gt;
  Button
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
  function showTab() {
    const triggerEl = document.getElementById('nav-voluteers-tab');
    const tab = new bootstrap.Tab(triggerEl);
    tab.show();
  }
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Or even simpler, no JS:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;button
  type=&quot;button&quot;
  class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;
  data-bs-toggle=&quot;tab&quot;
  data-bs-target=&quot;#nav-volunteers&quot;
&gt;
  Button
&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>But if you do that, make sure the target points to the pane id that actually exists, which in your markup is #nav-volunteers.</p>
